Section 31 — Merger Event Detection & Coalescence Tracking

Author: Abhinav Vatsa
Work time: ~10.5 hours handwritten implementation

Implemented a fully manual merger-event detection subsystem for the MW–M31 N-body simulation pipeline to determine the physical coalescence time of the Milky Way and Andromeda halos.

No AI-generated code was used in this section. Development was based structurally on patterns and architecture established in previous pipeline sections, but all merger-detection logic, diagnostics, tracking systems, thresholds, analysis routines, and visualization code were written manually.

Developed:

* center-of-mass separation tracking,
* relative velocity evolution analysis,
* dense-core overlap diagnostics,
* density-peak convergence detection,
* merger-threshold logic,
* automated final-coalescence identification.

Implemented physically motivated merger criteria requiring:

* persistent COM separation below a critical radius,
* irreversible orbital decay,
* substantial dense-core overlap,
* suppression of false-positive flyby detections.

Built visualization and diagnostics infrastructure for:

* separation evolution,
* orbital energy dissipation,
* merger phase-space trajectories,
* dense-core overlap evolution,
* dynamical merger-state analysis.

Key engineering work included:

* KD-tree nearest-neighbor overlap calculations,
* snapshot-by-snapshot merger-state validation,
* numerical stabilization of particle-selection routines,
* integration with existing MW–M31 analysis infrastructure,
* automated merger-epoch extraction.
